## Project Workflow

This project uses **Spec-Driven Development** enforced by SDDKit.
The workflow is: **spec → plan → tasks → implement → review**.

**Implementation is blocked until spec, plan, and tasks are human-approved.**
This is enforced by the `PreToolUse` hook in `.claude/hooks/pre_tool_use.py`.

## Commands Available

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `/spec` | Write a specification with REQ-NNN IDs |
| `/plan` | Write a technical plan citing every REQ-NNN |
| `/tasks` | Break the plan into implementation tasks |
| `/implement` | Implement approved tasks (gates enforced) |
| `/review` | Review against spec + optional domain pack |

## Validator Agent

A validator subagent lives in `.claude/agents/validator.md`.
It is a **supplemental reviewer** — not the primary enforcer.
The deterministic checker (`sddkit check`) is the primary enforcer.

## Approval Gates

Approval is managed by `sddkit approve <feature> <spec|plan|tasks>`.
Status is stored in `specs/<feature>/status.json`.
The hook reads this file before every source-file write.

## Audit Log

Every tool action is logged to `specs/<feature>/audit.jsonl`.
Read the report with: `sddkit report <feature>`

## Key Commands (for the human operator)

```bash
sddkit check <feature>          # Check requirement traceability
sddkit approve <feature> spec   # Approve the spec
sddkit approve <feature> plan   # Approve the plan
sddkit approve <feature> tasks  # Approve the tasks
sddkit report <feature>         # Summarise the audit log
sddkit eval                     # Run the eval harness (CI)
```

## Design Rule

> **Deterministic checks first, LLM second.**
> The traceability checker and approval gates are hard guarantees.
> The validator agent is an extra reviewer on top — never the only enforcer.
